{%- comment -%}
  fye-ring-finder — the step-by-step ring finder. 1 use: page.find-your-ring.

  When a journey returns NO rings the screen collapses to one column — the
  bespoke offer, with its own heading ("We'll design your ring for you") and
  its own opening line. A promise of matches above an empty grid, and an
  "Or," referring to nothing, would both be worse than saying the true thing
  (Ed, 04/09/2026).

  The RESULTS SCREEN offers two options of equal weight, side by side: the
  rings that match, and a bespoke enquiry. Neither is a card and both carry
  the same heading treatment — a border on one side would make the other
  read as the default (Ed, 04/09/2026). The question panels keep the narrow
  reading measure; only this screen uses the full width.

  REVISED 03/09/2026 (3), Ed: engagement and diamond journeys now open on a
  FORK — "start with the setting" or "start with the stone" — and metal is
  asked as colour first, then carat only if a gold was chosen.

  HOW IT WORKS
  · JOURNEY blocks (a collection each), optional FORK blocks, and one STEP
    block per question. A step belongs to a journey by matching `journey` keys.
    Everything renders into the HTML at once and hidden; fye-ui.js shows one
    panel at a time and appends a filter param per answer.

  · THE FORK does not add questions, it reorders them. Each step carries a
    `group` — setting, stone, or none — and the fork chooses which group is
    asked first. Ungrouped steps (metal, carat, coverage) always come last.
    So one set of step blocks serves both routes and there is nothing to keep
    in sync. A journey with no fork block runs in plain block order.
      eng, setting first:  style, shoulders, stone type, cut, size, metal
      eng, stone first:    stone type, cut, size, style, shoulders, metal
    The fork deliberately has NO "I'm flexible": it is a route, not a filter,
    and every route asks every question. It is also not counted as a step.

  · CONDITIONAL STEPS. A step with `when_param` + `when_value` is asked only
    if an earlier answer to `when_param` contains `when_value`. That is how
    carat works: asked only when the metal colour contains "Gold". The step
    total counts a pending conditional step optimistically, so a shopper who
    picks Platinum finishes one step early — the count never grows mid-journey,
    which is the direction that would feel like a moving target.

  · Options are a textarea, one per line:
        Label | value | icon.svg | note
    An icon of `swatch: Rose Gold` draws the theme's own metal swatch —
    the same one the filter rail uses — instead of loading a file. Any
    metal name fye-metal-swatch knows will do, with or without a carat.
    Value, icon and note are all optional; a missing value falls back to the
    label. One block per option would need ~90 blocks against Shopify's cap of
    50, so the textarea IS the editable list.

  · VALUE SYNTAX, read by fye-ui.js:
      Concave                       filter.p.m.filters.<param>=Concave
      1.00..1.49                    <param>.gte=1.00&<param>.lte=1.49  (either side may be empty)
      carat=18ct&metal_colour=Rose Gold   two params at once; the step's own
                                    param is ignored
    A param beginning `fye_` is CARRIED, not filtered: it stays out of the
    collection URL and travels with the enquiry instead. Metal is asked on
    every journey but only the plain collection can filter on it (Ed,
    14/08 and 03/09/2026).

  · ICONS. `icon_size` (40 / 56 / 88px) and `icon_style` per step. Line art
    fades a step on hover, because recolouring teal line-art would need a mask;
    colour art — the metal swatches, and product photography later — does not
    fade, because dimming a photograph looks like a fault. Swatches are square:
    the brand has no rounded corners outside the logo. Icons are files in
    Content › Files resolved with `file_url` (see fye-shape-tiles for why not
    image_picker), and fye-ui.js removes any that fail to load, so a filename
    typo costs a missing icon rather than a broken-image glyph.

  · JOURNEY TILES take a PRODUCT rather than an icon: a photograph of a
    representative ring identifies a category, where a 68px line drawing of
    a ring is a small grey circle whatever it depicts. The tile follows the
    product's featured image, so a re-shoot needs no theme change. Icons
    still work where no product is set.

  · Every step except the fork ends with "I'm flexible" (empty value, no
    param). That rule is what guarantees no ring is orphaned. Do not remove it.

  · The heading is deliberately absent from page.find-your-ring: the banner
    already names the page, and two titles a screen apart read as a mistake.
    The settings remain for other uses.

  · Without JavaScript each journey card is a plain link to its collection and
    the enquiry form still posts.

  Filters are LIVE and verified (Ed, 03/09/2026): all 12 `filters.*` metafields
  are on in Search & Discovery, and Concave + 4mm + 18ct Rose Gold returns
  exactly 3. The visible sidebar on the collection page is still xCloud's and
  will not show these filters as ticked.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign band = s.band | default: 'ivory'
  assign top = s.top_space | default: 'standard'
  assign journeys_all = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'journey'
  assign flex_label = s.flexible_label | default: "I'm flexible"
  assign journeys = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'journey'
  assign forks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'fork'
  assign steps = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'step'
-%}

<section class="rfd band band--{{ band }}{% if top == 'flush' %} band--flush-top{% elsif top == 'tight' %} rfd--tight-top{% endif %}"
         data-screen-label="Ring finder" data-fye-finder>
  {%- comment -%}
    The two gradients every metal swatch references. Once per page, and only
    here: fye-filter-icons emits the same two ids for the collection rail,
    and no page renders both.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'fye-metal-swatch', defs: true -%}
  <div class="wrap rfd__wrap">

    {%- if s.eyebrow != blank or s.heading != blank or s.intro != blank -%}
      <div class="sect-head rfd__head">
        {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}<p class="eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.heading != blank -%}<h2>{{ s.heading }}</h2>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.intro != blank -%}<p class="lead">{{ s.intro }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Hidden until a journey is chosen: on the first screen both children are
      empty and the row was holding 56px open. fye-ui.js reveals it, and the
      min-height then keeps the stage from shifting between steps.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="rfd__bar" data-fye-finder-bar hidden>
      <button type="button" class="rfd__back" data-fye-finder-back hidden>Back</button>
      <p class="rfd__progress eyebrow" data-fye-finder-progress hidden></p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Shopify posts the contact form back to this page with
      ?contact_posted=true. `posted_successfully?` is only readable inside a
      form block, and the real form sits inside the results panel — which is
      hidden on a fresh load — so this empty form block is how the section
      finds out. It emits no markup of its own.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign just_posted = false -%}
    {%- form 'contact', id: 'rfd-posted-probe' -%}
      {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}{%- assign just_posted = true -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endform -%}

    {%- if just_posted -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The whole stage is replaced. Restarting the finder underneath a
        thank-you would invite the same enquiry twice.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="rfd__stage" data-fye-finder-posted>
        <div class="rfd__panel rfd__thanks-panel">
          <h3 class="rfd__q" tabindex="-1">{{ s.custom_thanks_heading | default: 'Thank you — that is with us' }}</h3>
          <p class="rfd__hint">{{ s.custom_thanks | default: "Thank you. We'll be in touch shortly with options made for you." }}</p>
          <div class="rfd__ractions">
            <a class="btn btn--outline" href="{{ request.path }}">{{ s.restart_label | default: 'Start the finder again' }}</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
    <div class="rfd__stage">

      <div class="rfd__panel" data-fye-finder-panel="journeys">
        {%- if s.journeys_q != blank -%}
          <h3 class="rfd__q" tabindex="-1" data-fye-finder-question>{{ s.journeys_q }}</h3>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if journeys.size > 0 -%}
          <ul class="rfd__journeys">
            {%- for block in journeys -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign b = block.settings
                assign coll = b.collection
                assign jkey = b.key | default: coll.handle
              -%}
              <li class="rfd__jitem" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {%- liquid
                  assign shot = null
                  if b.product != blank and b.product.featured_image
                    assign shot = b.product.featured_image
                  endif
                -%}
                <a class="rfd__journey{% if shot %} rfd__journey--photo{% endif %}" href="{{ coll.url | default: '/collections/all' }}"
                   data-fye-finder-journey="{{ jkey }}"
                   data-fye-finder-collection="{{ coll.url | default: '/collections/all' }}"
                   data-fye-finder-label="{{ b.label | default: coll.title | escape }}">
                  {%- if shot -%}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Square, because ring photography is shot square and letting
                      each tile follow its own file is what made the old grids
                      ragged (see .pcard in fye-core). alt is empty: the tile's
                      own words name the category, and the ring in the picture is
                      an example rather than the subject.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <span class="rfd__jshot" style="--jinset: {{ b.inset | default: '0' }};">
                      <img src="{{ shot | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                           srcset="{{ shot | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ shot | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w"
                           sizes="(max-width: 560px) 90vw, (max-width: 900px) 45vw, 30vw"
                           alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy">
                    </span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span class="rfd__jwords">
                  {%- if shot -%}
                    {%- comment -%} A photograph replaces the icon; both would be noise. {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- elsif b.icon != blank -%}
                    <img class="rfd__jicon" src="{{ b.icon | file_url }}" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="68" height="68" loading="lazy" data-fye-finder-icon>
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      A tile with no icon beside tiles that have one starts its
                      text 68px higher, which is what made the plain wedding
                      rings card look broken. Hold the space instead — only
                      when a sibling has an icon at all.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- for j in journeys_all -%}
                      {%- if j.settings.icon != blank -%}
                        <span class="rfd__jicon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        {%- break -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span class="rfd__jname">{{ b.label | default: coll.title }}</span>
                  {%- if b.description != blank -%}
                    <span class="rfd__jdesc">{{ b.description }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                </a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- else -%}
          <p class="lead">Add a journey block for each collection the finder should search.</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- for block in forks -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign b = block.settings
          assign lines = b.options | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
          assign isize = b.icon_size | default: '56'
        -%}
        <div class="rfd__panel" hidden
             data-fye-finder-fork
             data-fye-finder-journey="{{ b.journey }}"
             {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <h3 class="rfd__q" tabindex="-1" data-fye-finder-question>{{ b.heading | default: 'Where would you like to start?' }}</h3>
          {%- if b.hint != blank -%}<p class="rfd__hint">{{ b.hint }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          <div class="rfd__fork" style="--isize: {{ isize }}px;">
            {%- for line in lines -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign row = line | strip
                if row == blank
                  continue
                endif
                assign parts = row | split: '|'
                assign lbl = parts[0] | strip
                assign val = parts[1] | strip
                assign ico = parts[2] | strip
                assign note = parts[3] | strip
              -%}
              <button type="button" class="rfd__opt rfd__opt--fork rfd__opt--{{ b.icon_style | default: 'line' }}"
                      data-fye-finder-route="{{ val | escape }}">
                {%- if ico contains 'swatch:' -%}
                  {%- assign metal = ico | remove_first: 'swatch:' | strip -%}
                  {%- render 'fye-metal-swatch', metal: metal, class: 'rfd__oicon' -%}
                {%- elsif ico != blank -%}
                  <img class="rfd__oicon" src="{{ ico | file_url }}" alt="" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" data-fye-finder-icon>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="rfd__olabel">{{ lbl }}</span>
                {%- if note != blank -%}<span class="rfd__onote">{{ note }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- for block in steps -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign b = block.settings
          assign cols = b.columns | default: '3'
          assign isize = b.icon_size | default: '56'
          assign lines = b.options | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
        -%}
        <fieldset class="rfd__panel rfd__step" hidden
                  data-fye-finder-step
                  data-fye-finder-journey="{{ b.journey }}"
                  data-fye-finder-group="{{ b.group }}"
                  data-fye-finder-param="{{ b.param }}"
                  data-fye-finder-when-param="{{ b.when_param }}"
                  data-fye-finder-when-value="{{ b.when_value }}"
                  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <legend class="rfd__q" tabindex="-1" data-fye-finder-question>{{ b.heading | default: 'Choose an option' }}</legend>
          {%- if b.hint != blank -%}<p class="rfd__hint">{{ b.hint }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          <div class="rfd__opts" style="--cols: {{ cols }}; --isize: {{ isize }}px;">
            {%- for line in lines -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign row = line | strip
                if row == blank
                  continue
                endif
                assign parts = row | split: '|'
                assign lbl = parts[0] | strip
                assign val = parts[1] | strip | default: lbl
                assign ico = parts[2] | strip
                assign note = parts[3] | strip
              -%}
              <button type="button" class="rfd__opt rfd__opt--{{ b.icon_style | default: 'line' }}"
                      data-fye-finder-option
                      data-fye-finder-value="{{ val | escape }}"
                      data-fye-finder-label="{{ lbl | escape }}">
                {%- if ico contains 'swatch:' -%}
                  {%- assign metal = ico | remove_first: 'swatch:' | strip -%}
                  {%- render 'fye-metal-swatch', metal: metal, class: 'rfd__oicon' -%}
                {%- elsif ico != blank -%}
                  <img class="rfd__oicon" src="{{ ico | file_url }}" alt="" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" data-fye-finder-icon>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="rfd__olabel">{{ lbl }}</span>
                {%- if note != blank -%}<span class="rfd__onote">{{ note }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
            <button type="button" class="rfd__opt rfd__opt--flex"
                    data-fye-finder-option
                    data-fye-finder-value=""
                    data-fye-finder-label="{{ flex_label | escape }}">
              <span class="rfd__olabel">{{ flex_label }}</span>
            </button>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      {%- endfor -%}

      <div class="rfd__panel rfd__results" hidden data-fye-finder-panel="results">

        {%- comment -%}
          Your answers first, spanning both columns: they belong to the whole
          screen, not to either option.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="rfd__chips" data-fye-finder-chips></p>

        <div class="rfd__two">
          <section class="rfd__opt-col rfd__col--rings">
            <h3 class="rfd__q" tabindex="-1" data-fye-finder-question>{{ s.results_heading | default: 'Here are the rings that match' }}</h3>
            <p class="rfd__count" data-fye-finder-count aria-live="polite"></p>
            <div class="rfd__grid" data-fye-finder-grid></div>
            <div class="rfd__ractions">
              <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/collections/all" data-fye-finder-results hidden>{{ s.results_label | default: 'See all matching rings' }}</a>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="rfd__opt-col rfd__custom">
            {%- comment -%}
              Two headings, one per state. With matching rings this column is
              the second of two options, so it opens "Or,". With none it is
              the only option, and "Or," would refer to nothing.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <h3 class="rfd__q" data-fye-finder-ctitle="some">{{ s.custom_heading | default: "Or, let's design your perfect ring for you" }}</h3>
            <p class="rfd__hint" data-fye-finder-ctitle="some">{{ s.custom_intro | default: "Tell us what you had in mind and we'll come back to you with custom options." }}</p>
            <h3 class="rfd__q" tabindex="-1" data-fye-finder-ctitle="none" hidden>{{ s.empty_heading | default: "We'll design your ring for you" }}</h3>
            <p class="rfd__hint" data-fye-finder-ctitle="none" hidden>{{ s.empty_intro | default: "Nothing in stock matches every answer you gave — which simply means yours is a ring we make rather than one we hold. Leave your details and we'll come back to you with designs and a price." }}</p>
          {%- form 'contact', class: 'rfd__form', id: 'rfd-enquiry' -%}
            {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
              <p class="rfd__thanks">{{ s.custom_thanks | default: "Thank you. We'll be in touch shortly with options made for you." }}</p>
            {%- else -%}
              {%- if form.errors -%}
                <p class="rfd__error">{{ form.errors | default_errors }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              <div class="rfd__fields">
                <p class="rfd__field">
                  <label for="rfd-name">Name</label>
                  <input type="text" id="rfd-name" name="contact[name]" autocomplete="name" required>
                </p>
                <p class="rfd__field">
                  <label for="rfd-email">Email</label>
                  <input type="email" id="rfd-email" name="contact[email]" autocomplete="email" required>
                </p>
                <p class="rfd__field">
                  <label for="rfd-phone">Telephone <span class="rfd__opt-note">optional</span></label>
                  <input type="tel" id="rfd-phone" name="contact[phone]" autocomplete="tel">
                </p>
                <p class="rfd__field rfd__field--wide">
                  <label for="rfd-body">What are you looking for?</label>
                  <textarea id="rfd-body" name="contact[body]" rows="3" placeholder="{{ s.custom_placeholder | default: 'Anything you would like us to know — a stone, a budget, a date.' | escape }}"></textarea>
                </p>
              </div>
              <input type="hidden" name="contact[Ring finder]" value="" data-fye-finder-answers-field>
              <button type="submit" class="btn">{{ s.custom_label | default: 'Send my details' }}</button>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endform -%}
          </section>
        </div>

        <button type="button" class="rfd__restart" data-fye-finder-restart>Start again</button>

      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.fye .rfd__wrap { max-width: var(--maxw); }
.fye .rfd__head { margin-bottom: var(--s6); }
/* Set the token, never a padding declaration (core rule 1). */
.fye .rfd--tight-top { padding-block-start: var(--sect-y-tight); }
/* Questions are a reading measure; only the two-option results screen uses
   the full width. Centring them inside a wide wrap keeps one wrapper for
   the section rather than two competing measures. */
.fye .rfd__bar,
.fye .rfd__panel:not(.rfd__results) { max-width: var(--maxw-narrow); margin-inline: auto; width: 100%; }

/* Back + progress share one row so the stage below never moves when the
   back button appears. min-height holds the row when both are hidden. */
.fye .rfd__bar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
  min-height: 44px;
  margin-bottom: var(--s3);
}
.fye .rfd__progress { margin: 0; margin-left: auto; }
.fye .rfd__back {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-button);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .rfd__back:hover { color: var(--sage); }
.fye .rfd__back[hidden], .fye .rfd__progress[hidden] { display: none; }
.fye .rfd__bar[hidden] { display: none; }

.fye .rfd__panel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s5); }
.fye .rfd__panel[hidden] { display: none; }
.fye .rfd__step { margin: 0; padding: 0; border: 0; min-width: 0; }

/* The question. Display face at the h3 size, sentence case: it is a question
   put to one person, not a section title. */
.fye .rfd__q {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-h3);
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  line-height: var(--lh-heading);
  text-transform: none;
  color: var(--ink);
}
.fye .rfd__q:focus { outline: none; }
.fye .rfd__hint { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }

/* --- journeys ------------------------------------------------------------ */
.fye .rfd__journeys {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--grid-gap);
}
.fye .rfd__jitem { margin: 0; display: flex; }
.fye .rfd__journey {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--s3);
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: var(--s5);
  border: var(--hairline);
  background: var(--white);
  color: var(--ink);
  transition: border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .rfd__journey:hover { border-color: var(--sage); color: var(--ink); }
.fye .rfd__journey:hover .rfd__jname { color: var(--sage); }
.fye .rfd__jicon { width: 68px; height: 68px; }
/* Photograph tiles: the image reaches the tile edges and the words sit in
   their own padded block, which is the product card's idiom (.pcard) rather
   than an image framed by padding. */
.fye .rfd__journey--photo { padding: 0; gap: 0; overflow: hidden; }
/* The BOX is the square, so the inset has something to hold. Photography
   arrives cropped differently — WBM3-YEL has margin around the band, ENG6162
   and FET8068 are cropped close — and at the same display size that reads as
   three different photographers. The inset is display padding only: it does
   not touch the files, which appear elsewhere on the site. */
.fye .rfd__jshot {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  padding: var(--jinset, 0);
  /* White, not ivory: the inset exposes this ground, and ivory read as a grey
     square inside a white tile. Ivory is right for a full-bleed product image
     (.pcard__media) where it is only ever seen through a transparent PNG. */
  background: var(--white);
  overflow: hidden;
}
.fye .rfd__jshot :where(img) {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: contain;
  transition: transform var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
/* The brand allows a gentle scale on product imagery, and nothing more. */
.fye .rfd__journey--photo:hover .rfd__jshot :where(img) { transform: scale(1.03); }
.fye .rfd__jwords {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--s3);
}
.fye .rfd__journey--photo .rfd__jwords { padding: var(--s5); }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .fye .rfd__journey--photo:hover .rfd__jshot :where(img) { transform: none; }
}
.fye .rfd__jname {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  letter-spacing: 0.07em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .rfd__jdesc { font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); }

/* --- options ------------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .rfd__opts {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--cols, 3), minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--s3);
}
/* Two tiles, roomier than a step's, because this choice sets the whole route. */
.fye .rfd__fork {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--s4);
}
/* A tile, not a button: white ground, hairline, the label in body type. The
   hover shifts the edge and the words to sage, like every other control. */
.fye .rfd__opt {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: var(--s2);
  min-height: 56px;
  padding: var(--s4);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  background: var(--white);
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  font-weight: var(--fw-regular);
  line-height: 1.35;
  text-align: center;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color var(--dur) var(--ease), color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .rfd__opt:hover { border-color: var(--sage); color: var(--sage); }
.fye .rfd__opt:active { border-color: var(--sage-deep); color: var(--sage-deep); }
.fye .rfd__opt--fork { gap: var(--s3); padding: var(--s5); }
.fye .rfd__onote { font-size: var(--fs-fine); font-weight: var(--fw-light); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.fye .rfd__oicon { width: var(--isize, 56px); height: var(--isize, 56px); }
/* Teal line-art fades a step on hover; a recolour would need a mask. Colour
   art — metal swatches, photography — never fades: a dimmed photograph reads
   as a fault rather than a hover. */
.fye .rfd__opt--line:hover .rfd__oicon { opacity: 0.7; }
.fye .rfd__opt--colour .rfd__oicon { border: var(--hairline); }
.fye .rfd__opt--flex {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
  background: transparent;
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

/* --- results ------------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .rfd__results { gap: var(--s6); }
/* Two options, equal weight: same heading, same column width, one hairline
   between them. Neither is a card — a bordered box on one side would make
   the other look like the default. Ed, 04/09/2026. */
.fye .rfd__two {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--s10);
  align-items: start;
}
.fye .rfd__opt-col {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s4);
  min-width: 0;
  padding-top: var(--s5);
  border-top: var(--hairline);
}
/* No rings matched. The grid and its heading go, and the bespoke offer —
   now the only option — takes the reading measure rather than sitting in a
   half-width column beside nothing. */
.fye .rfd__results[data-fye-finder-empty] .rfd__col--rings { display: none; }
.fye .rfd__results[data-fye-finder-empty] .rfd__two {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  max-width: var(--maxw-narrow);
  margin-inline: auto;
  width: 100%;
}
.fye .rfd__two [data-fye-finder-ctitle][hidden] { display: none; }
/* The answers as one quiet line under the heading, not a definition list:
   at this point in the journey they are context, not the subject. */
.fye .rfd__chips { margin: 0; font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--ink-soft); }
.fye .rfd__count {
  margin: 0;
  padding-bottom: var(--s3);
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-button);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}
.fye .rfd__grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--s6) var(--grid-gap);
}
.fye .rfd__grid > :where(div) { display: contents; }
.fye .rfd-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s2);
  color: var(--ink);
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .rfd-card:hover { color: var(--sage); }
.fye .rfd-card__media {
  display: block;
  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
  background: var(--white);
  overflow: hidden;
}
.fye .rfd-card__media :where(img) { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; }
.fye .rfd-card__title { font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.4; }
.fye .rfd-card__price { font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--ink-soft); }
.fye .rfd__ractions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: var(--s5); }
.fye .rfd__restart {
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-button);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .rfd__restart:hover { color: var(--sage); }

/* --- custom enquiry ------------------------------------------------------ */
.fye .rfd__form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s4); margin: 0; }
/* One column: the enquiry now lives in half the page. */
.fye .rfd__fields {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--s3);
}
.fye .rfd__field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s1); margin: 0; }
.fye .rfd__field--wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
.fye .rfd__field :where(label) {
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-button);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}
.fye .rfd__opt-note { font-weight: var(--fw-light); letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none; }
.fye .rfd__field :where(input, textarea) {
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: var(--s2) var(--s3);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  background: var(--white);
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  transition: border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .rfd__field :where(textarea) { min-height: 88px; resize: vertical; }
.fye .rfd__field :where(input:focus, textarea:focus) { border-color: var(--sage); outline: none; }
.fye .rfd__form :where(.btn) { align-self: flex-start; }
.fye .rfd__thanks, .fye .rfd__error { margin: 0; font-size: var(--fs-small); }
/* The post-submit panel. Reading measure, like the questions it replaces. */
.fye .rfd__thanks-panel { max-width: var(--maxw-narrow); margin-inline: auto; width: 100%; gap: var(--s4); }
.fye .rfd__error { color: var(--sage-deep); }

/* --- breakpoints, last --------------------------------------------------- */
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .fye .rfd__opts { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .fye .rfd__two { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s8); }
  .fye .rfd__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .fye .rfd__fields { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .rfd__journeys { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .fye .rfd__fork { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .fye .rfd__opts { gap: var(--s2); }
  .fye .rfd__opt { padding: var(--s3); }
  .fye .rfd__opt--fork { padding: var(--s4); }
  .fye .rfd__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .fye .rfd__fields { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .fye .rfd__ractions { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--s3); }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
